/**
\page org_mitk_views_simpleregistrationview Registration

This view registers a moving image to a fixed image with a rigid or an affine transformation
(MatchPoint's multi-modal default algorithms), and applies a registration to a tractogram.

<b>Image Registration</b>: choose the fixed and the moving image and the <b>Registration Type</b>,
then press <b>Start Registration</b>. For a diffusion-weighted image (DWI), the spin box next to it
selects the volume used to compute the registration. The result appears as a new image named
after the moving image:

\li A rigid registration only moves the geometry of the moving image, without resampling, unless
<b>Always Resample to Target</b> is checked. An affine registration always resamples the moving
image onto the grid of the fixed image, with B-spline interpolation.
\li All volumes of a moving DWI are mapped, and its gradient directions are rotated with the
image.
\li With <b>Output Registration Object</b> the registration is also added to the Data Manager, for
example to transform a tractogram later.

Only one registration runs at a time; if it fails, a message shows the reason.

<b>Tractography Registration</b>: choose a tractogram and a registration object and press
<b>Start Tractography Registration</b>. The transformed tractogram appears below the input, named
"_registered". Only affine (including rigid) registrations can be applied to tractograms.

*/
